    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add a video (or photo) segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT     Resource: local:///<abs_path> or vimo://<id>; smart_colors\r\n                              accepts vimo:// only\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --width TEXT        Media width in px. Canonical unit: px; the px suffix is preferred\r\n                              and bare px values remain accepted. Range after normalization:\r\n                              [1,2147483647]. Whole-number value required.\r\n          --height TEXT       Media height in px. Canonical unit: px; the px suffix is\r\n                              preferred and bare px values remain accepted. Range after\r\n                              normalization: [1,2147483647]. Whole-number value required.\r\n          --is-photo TEXT     Treat resource as a still image (true/false)\r\n          --render-index TEXT Render layer index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a video clip from a local file\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video add --resource local:///x/y.mp4\r\n  # Add a still image as a 3s photo segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video add --resource local:///x/y.jpg --is-photo true --duration 3s\r\n",
